problems.problem:
For which of the following values of $A, B, C$ does the system $$\begin{cases} (x - y)(z - t)(z - x)(z - t)^2 = A, \\ (y - z)(t - x)(t - y)(x - z)^2 = B, \\ (x - z)(y - t)(z - t)(y - z)^2 = C \end{cases}$$ have a solution in real numbers, and for which does it not?

(a) $A = 2$, $B = 8$, $C = 6$;

(b) $A = 2$, $B = 6$, $C = 8$.

Let $M = \{1, 2, \ldots, n\}$, and let $S_i$ denote the set of all $i$-element subsets of $M$, for $0 \le i \le n$. Suppose that $k < n/2$. Prove that there exists a function $f : S_k \to S_{k+1}$ satisfying the following conditions:

(a) if $X, Y \in S_k$ and $X \ne Y$, then $f(X) \ne f(Y)$;

(b) $X \subset f(X)$ for every $X \in S_k$.

An acute triangle $ABC$ is inscribed in a circle with center $O$. Point $P$ lies on the minor arc $AB$. The line through $P$ perpendicular to $BO$ intersects sides $AB$ and $BC$ at $S$ and $T$, respectively. The line through $P$ perpendicular to $AO$ intersects sides $AB$ and $AC$ at $Q$ and $R$, respectively. Prove that:

(a) triangles $PQS$ and $PQR$ have equal areas;

(b) $PQ^2 = QR \cdot ST$.
